{"document":2,"title":"assistant in #88432d0a:sharegpt_HpkiAOb_9: Sure, here's the revised blog post incorporating a...","updated_at":"2023-05-23T19:14:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"* 1/2 cup blue cheese, crumbled * 2 large eggs * 2 teaspoons vanilla extract * 2 cups semisweet chocolate chips Instructions: 1. Preheat your oven to 375°F (190°C). Line a baking sheet with parchment paper. 2. In a bowl, whisk together flour, baking soda, and salt. 3. In a separate bowl, use an electric mixer to cream the butter, sugar, and blue cheese until light and fluffy. 4. Beat in the eggs and vanilla extract. 5. Gradually mix in the flour mixture until well combined. 6. Fold in the chocolate chips. 7. Drop the dough by tablespoonfuls onto the prepared baking sheet. 8. Bake for 12-15 minutes, or until the edges are lightly golden. 9. Remove the cookies from the oven and allow them to cool on the baking sheet for 5 minutes before transferring them to a wire rack to cool completely. So next time you're in the mood for something sweet and savory, give these Blue Cheese Chocolate Chip Cookies a try. You might even surprise yourself, or your picky eaters like my son did! I promise you won't be disappointed!","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"88432d0a:sharegpt_HpkiAOb_9\"}"}
